What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/10204000.spm-suspend/wake_after_ms
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        X20 Bring-up <x20@localhost>
Description:
                Optional PCM sleep timer for the next system deep suspend,
                in milliseconds: 0 disables the timer (default), otherwise
                100..600000. Other enabled hardware wake sources remain armed.
                Select deep in /sys/power/mem_sleep, then write mem to
                /sys/power/state. This attribute does not start suspend.

What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/10204000.spm-suspend/state
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        X20 Bring-up <x20@localhost>
Description:
                Read-only cycle/resume/error counts, PCM ownership/reset safety,
                DCM lease and last raw wake/debug/timer/flag records. A resume
                count requires the PSCI warm cpu_resume path. CPU powerdown is
                implemented; INFRA powerdown is requested but physical INFRA
                shutdown is not verified on this board. Manual CPU rails are
                retained. These fields are diagnostics, not power measurements.
                CIRQ records clone/resume cycles, replayed pending lines, its
                enabled state and the last seven pending words (SPI72..290).
                Original CIRQ polarity, sensitivity, mask and control settings
                are restored after replaying retained interrupts into the GIC.
